  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "41159676",
      "title": "Optimizing Images with the NextJS Image Component",
      "lectureOrder": 100,
      "videoOrder": 93,
      "sourceHash": "c632ee1cd6b81f59ef88baff8179693550fbc809911197649010e9d00f490bf6",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.9,
          "end": 3.84,
          "en": "So, now that we styled this header,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.84,
          "end": 7.35,
          "en": "there's another element of this header that can be improved",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.35,
          "end": 9.723,
          "en": "and that would be this image here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.16,
          "end": 12.36,
          "en": "Because at the moment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.36,
          "end": 15.21,
          "en": "we're simply using the regular image element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.21,
          "end": 17.64,
          "en": "for displaying this image.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.64,
          "end": 22.5,
          "en": "And that's not bad or a problem, but in NextJS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.5,
          "end": 25.02,
          "en": "you actually got a better element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.02,
          "end": 29.19,
          "en": "for outputting images than this default image element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.19,
          "end": 30.66,
          "en": "Because in NextJS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.66,
          "end": 33.81,
          "en": "you have a special built-in image component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.81,
          "end": 36.99,
          "en": "which exists to help you output images",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.99,
          "end": 39.48,
          "en": "in a more optimized way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.48,
          "end": 43.17,
          "en": "For example, by lazy loading images under the hood",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.17,
          "end": 44.73,
          "en": "so that they're only displayed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.73,
          "end": 46.83,
          "en": "if they're really visible on the page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 46.83,
          "end": 48.78,
          "en": "It does that automatically for you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 48.78,
          "end": 51.75,
          "en": "without any extra configuration.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 51.75,
          "end": 53.97,
          "en": "It can also simplify the process",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 53.97,
          "end": 57.3,
          "en": "of setting up responsive images and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 57.3,
          "end": 59.25,
          "en": "And therefore, the recommendation is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 59.25,
          "end": 62.73,
          "en": "to use this image component in your NextJS projects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 62.73,
          "end": 64.953,
          "en": "if you are outputting any image.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 66.06,
          "end": 68.97,
          "en": "Now, this image component has a lot of props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 68.97,
          "end": 71.07,
          "en": "and configuration options,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 71.07,
          "end": 74.22,
          "en": "and attached you find a link to the full article",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 74.22,
          "end": 75.57,
          "en": "on this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 75.57,
          "end": 77.61,
          "en": "Though I will say that many of those props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 77.61,
          "end": 81.57300000000001,
          "en": "and options are really for more advanced use cases.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 83.55,
          "end": 86.78999999999999,
          "en": "In general, getting started with that image component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 86.78999999999999,
          "end": 89.97,
          "en": "and using it in most use cases is pretty simple",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 89.97,
          "end": 91.56,
          "en": "and straightforward.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 91.56,
          "end": 94.62,
          "en": "And all you have to do here in this main header component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 94.62,
          "end": 99.62,
          "en": "is to replace the default IMG element here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 99.69,
          "end": 102.33,
          "en": "with the image element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 102.33,
          "end": 105.813,
          "en": "that can be imported from next/image.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 108.42,
          "end": 112.38,
          "en": "Then you need to set the source to such an imported image,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 112.38,
          "end": 114.9,
          "en": "but now to that overall object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 114.9,
          "end": 118.473,
          "en": "and not just the src property value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 119.43,
          "end": 122.913,
          "en": "So I changed that src prop value therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 124.14,
          "end": 127.44,
          "en": "because this object that's generated by NextJS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 127.44,
          "end": 128.85,
          "en": "when you import an image like,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 128.85,
          "end": 131.19,
          "en": "this contains useful information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 131.19,
          "end": 134.16,
          "en": "that's used under the hood by this image component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 134.16,
          "end": 136.593,
          "en": "to display it in an optimized way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 137.73,
          "end": 140.19,
          "en": "For example, it automatically detects the size",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 140.19,
          "end": 143.61,
          "en": "of this image, and therefore, in its simplest form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 143.61,
          "end": 145.11,
          "en": "this is all we have to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 145.11,
          "end": 147.303,
          "en": "No other setup is required.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 148.35,
          "end": 152.01,
          "en": "With that, if you reload, you will see the image as before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 152.01,
          "end": 153.69,
          "en": "but if you now inspect it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 153.69,
          "end": 155.88,
          "en": "you will see that this image element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 155.88,
          "end": 159.84,
          "en": "that's being rendered here has a couple of extra attributes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 159.84,
          "end": 161.57999999999998,
          "en": "which we didn't add.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 161.57999999999998,
          "end": 165.18,
          "en": "For example, this loading lazy attribute,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 165.18,
          "end": 168.09,
          "en": "which makes sure that the image is lazy loaded,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 168.09,
          "end": 170.853,
          "en": "and therefore, only loaded if it's really visible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 172.32,
          "end": 175.44,
          "en": "In addition, it automatically inferred the width and height,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 175.44,
          "end": 178.47,
          "en": "though we could overwrite that if you wanted to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 178.47,
          "end": 181.71,
          "en": "And it's generated this source set attribute here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 181.71,
          "end": 186.03,
          "en": "hence ensuring that differently sized images are loaded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 186.03,
          "end": 188.07,
          "en": "depending on the viewport",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 188.07,
          "end": 191.193,
          "en": "and the device we are using to visit this website.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 192.39,
          "end": 195.39,
          "en": "In addition, it will also automatically serve that image",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 195.39,
          "end": 197.94,
          "en": "in the best file format for the browser",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 197.94,
          "end": 199.95,
          "en": "that's being used by a user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 199.95,
          "end": 202.82999999999998,
          "en": "so for example, as a WebP image,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 202.82999999999998,
          "end": 205.62,
          "en": "if you're visiting this page with Chrome.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 205.62,
          "end": 207.72,
          "en": "As you can see if you visit the Network tab",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 207.72,
          "end": 208.77,
          "en": "and reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 208.77,
          "end": 211.82999999999998,
          "en": "there you'll see that this image that's being served here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 211.82999999999998,
          "end": 214.23,
          "en": "was returned as a WebP image,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 214.23,
          "end": 215.94,
          "en": "which is a special file format",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 215.94,
          "end": 218.163,
          "en": "that is more efficient than a PNG.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 220.11,
          "end": 221.97,
          "en": "And you get all of that out of the box",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 221.97,
          "end": 223.57,
          "en": "when using this image component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 225.06,
          "end": 227.22,
          "en": "Now, one thing we should do here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 227.22,
          "end": 230.37,
          "en": "about which we also learn here in the console,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 230.37,
          "end": 234.87,
          "en": "the JavaScript console, is add the priority property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 234.87,
          "end": 237.51,
          "en": "to this image since it will always be visible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 237.51,
          "end": 238.82999999999998,
          "en": "when this page loads.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 238.82999999999998,
          "end": 241.5,
          "en": "So lazy loading doesn't make a lot of sense here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 241.5,
          "end": 244.32,
          "en": "and we want to tell NextJS and the browser",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 244.32,
          "end": 246.33,
          "en": "that this image should always be loaded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 246.33,
          "end": 248.79,
          "en": "as quickly as possible to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 248.79,
          "end": 251.1,
          "en": "that we got no unnecessary content shift",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 251.1,
          "end": 253.323,
          "en": "or flickering when the page loads.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 254.19,
          "end": 256.35,
          "en": "Therefore, on this image component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 256.35,
          "end": 260.25,
          "en": "I'll now also add the priority property, like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 260.25,
          "end": 263.133,
          "en": "to make sure that this is loaded with priority.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 265.68,
          "end": 268.14,
          "en": "With that added, if we save that and reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 268.14,
          "end": 272.103,
          "en": "the page still looks as before, but this warning went away.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 273.3,
          "end": 276.723,
          "en": "And that is how we can use this image component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 277.83,
          "end": 280.83,
          "en": "Now as mentioned, you can definitely dive in deeper",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 280.83,
          "end": 284.15999999999997,
          "en": "to explore all the different use cases of this component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 284.15999999999997,
          "end": 286.83,
          "en": "and all the different configuration options.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 286.83,
          "end": 289.02,
          "en": "For example, also, if you're loading images",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 289.02,
          "end": 290.61,
          "en": "from a third party website",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 290.61,
          "end": 294.06,
          "en": "or anything like this, here for this website,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 294.06,
          "end": 295.623,
          "en": "this is all we have to do.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
